@* The `MainLayout` does not support Blazor Static SSR.
   Therefore, `App.razor` passes this layout to `Routes.razor`, where `<LayoutView />` uses it whenever
   `@rendermode` is null. That happens in two cases:
   - `WebAppRender:BlazorMode` is `BlazorSsr`, which applies to the WHOLE app - every page renders with this
     layout, so the app has no header, nav or menu at all. That is what "no interactivity" costs.
   - a page is marked `@attribute [ExcludeFromInteractiveRouting]`, which is the supported way to add a
     static SSR page to an otherwise interactive app. No page in this template uses it yet; this layout is
     what makes it work when one does. *@

@inherits LayoutComponentBase

@* MainLayout - and with it AppHeadCoordinator, which normally hosts this outlet - never renders here, so this layout
   hosts it instead. The two are mutually exclusive by construction, so the document still has only one of them. *@
<HeadContent>
    <SectionOutlet SectionName="@AppPageData.HeadSectionName" />
</HeadContent>

@Body
